// The diagnostic codes. Every code the compiler reports is named here once, and call sites pass the name:
//
//     diag_error_code(DIAG_CLI_CHECK_MISSING_SOURCE, "missing source file")
//
// A code is a promise to the people who read it in a log, a test or the documentation, so it must stay the
// same text when the code around it moves. Writing it at the call site made that depend on every author
// typing the right digits and never reusing a number; here it is one line a reader can look up, and
// `tools/lint.py` holds the registry to it: each name used at exactly one call site, each code written
// once, each code in the area of the file that reports it, and no `"Pnnnn"` literal anywhere else in
// `src/`.
//
// Names are `DIAG_<AREA>_<WHAT WENT WRONG>`, in code order within an area. Add the next free number in the
// area, never reuse one, and do not renumber: a code retired from the compiler stays retired.
//
// This module imports nothing, so `common.diagnostics` can use it without a cycle.

// --- P1xxx: the command line, the project commands, the driver and the formatter --

